From 7d61ec26c8946002222e6d2f2aa08c49b05cfd17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Niedermayer <michael@niedermayer.cc>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:39:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/flacdec: do not flush the parser on a zero length
 read in flac_read_timestamp()

A read that returns no data because the input reported EOF transiently
was passed to the parser as the EOF flush, the data of the next read was
then parsed by the flushed parser.

Fixes: NULL pointer dereference
Fixes: iEqlwpm7chzS
Found during the review of https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/24909
NULL pointer dereference Replicated through API with ASAN

(cherry picked from commit 7d61ec26c8946002222e6d2f2aa08c49b05cfd17)
---
 libavformat/flacdec.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavformat/flacdec.c b/libavformat/flacdec.c
index 8d907bdc3068..12d4b7305f77 100644
--- a/libavformat/flacdec.c
+++ b/libavformat/flacdec.c
@@ -311,6 +311,10 @@ av_unused static int64_t flac_read_timestamp(AVFormatContext *s, int stream_inde
 
         if (ret >= 0 || ret == AVERROR(EAGAIN))
             ret = ff_raw_read_partial_packet(s, pkt);
+        if (!ret) {
+            av_packet_unref(pkt);
+            continue;
+        }
         if (ret < 0){
             if (ret == AVERROR(EAGAIN))
                 continue;
